{"id": 20, "ts": 1780643394.5179856, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with Sarah that the lack of concrete evidence on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication is a critical gap. While D shows strong responsibility, problem\u2011solving and concentration, his moody, loner reputation raises doubts about how he would integrate into a cockpit crew over long\u2011haul flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC offers documented crew\u2011fit: he \u201cputs concern for others above everything,\u201d which directly supports the crew\u2011cooperation criterion, and he \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d addressing decision quality under pressure. His \u201cexcellent attention skills\u201d also cover the attention\u2011accuracy requirement. Although C has communication difficulties and an egocentric style, the evidence we have shows he creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, which is essential for safety\u2011critical teamwork. Given that D\u2019s cooperation and communication remain unknown, I would move my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC** as the best overall fit at this stage."}
