{"id": 29, "ts": 1780643509.6506062, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m aligning my provisional recommendation with James and Emily and moving to **Candidate\u202fC**.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fD brings strong responsibility, problem\u2011solving, concentration and an adequate response to unexpected events, we still have no concrete evidence on his crew\u2011cooperation or professional communication\u2014both are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011haul cockpit teamwork. Moreover, his reputation for arrogance and weak leadership raises further doubts about his ability to sustain a collaborative environment over extended flights.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, checks multiple critical boxes with documented evidence:\u202f100\u202f% reliability, creates a positive atmosphere with his crew (demonstrating crew\u2011cooperation), makes correct decisions quickly (decision quality), stays calm in a crisis (stress resilience), understands complicated technology (technical competence), and has excellent attention skills (attention & information accuracy). Although he has communication difficulties and an egocentric style, the fact that he \u201cputs concern for others above everything\u201d and fosters a positive crew environment suggests these issues are mitigated in practice. Given the concrete strengths across the core safety criteria and the lack of comparable data for D, Candidate\u202fC appears the safer overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
